= The Founding Inquiry

The Founding Inquiry has been an intermittent Assembly committee examining the chaos of the Founding: the collapse of the Empire after the God-Emperor's death, and whether the Commonwealth's founders betrayed the new Empress Jacqueline or saved the realm from ruin. So far it has faced massive resistance from the military establishment[? if president == "DuFour":&nbsp;up to President DuFour?].

- @restart: Restart the inquiry.
- @root: Do nothing.
- @easy_discard
- @cancel_advisor_action

@restart
on-arrival: war_guilt += 1

What is the goal of this tribunal?

- @pure_history: To provide a historical record of the events of the Founding.
- @rewrite: To revise the popular Commonwealth histories and finally put to rest the "stabbed in the back" myth.

@pure_history
on-arrival: dufour_angry -= 5

The history is being compiled, as it always has been.

@rewrite
on-arrival: pacifism += 1; nationalism -= 5*(1-dissent); pro_republic += 5*(1-dissent); coup_progress += 1; gold_left += 1; ddp_left += 0.5; lvp_left += 1; dufour_angry += 10

Destroying the "stabbed in the back" myth, in addition to finally correcting the historical record, would do a great deal to improve our party's reputation. This is why it would be resisted by the military establishment every step of the way.
